    "The comparison separates two sources of difficulty: which configurations are evaluated, and whether those configurations are supplied by a reference calculation or generated by the model itself. Thermal sampling, migration, and sliding probe different parts of the energy landscape; fixed paths test energy assignments, whereas MLIP-relaxed paths and MD expose feedback between predictions and the configurations sampled next. We use these complementary tests to ask when accuracy transfers across processes, rather than to produce a universal ranking of training strategies.",
